UADBB “GrECo Lietuva” – the second largest insurance brokerage company in Lithuania, with roots dating back to 1996, and since 2019 – a part of the Austrian risk and insurance brokerage company GrECo Group in Lithuania
“GrECo Group” is a leading broker in the Baltic States also Central and Eastern Europe, operating in more than 200 countries worldwide.
We manage risk and are trusted, loyal partner in all matters, offering progressive and tailored solutions. Our team consists of a wide spectrum of specialists with a high level of competence, and we aim to extend it to cope with increasing demand and responsibilities.
We are currently looking for a proactive, analytical and process – oriented team member to join us in the role of : IT Administrator / Key User with the focus on IT process management, system integrations & optimisation.
What will you be doing?:
In this role, you’ll ensure the smooth operation, optimisation and development of our IT systems, acting as the key link between users, external providers and the GrECo Group IT teams.
This is a position focused on process management, system functionality, integration coordination and supporting digital workflows.
Your Responsibilities:
IT process & project management and continuous improvement - map, standardize and refine core‑system processes, ensure alignment with SDLC, security standards and Group guidelines, contribute to projects requiring IT expertise;
Coordination, implementation and maintenance of office hardware and software (at the process level) - monitor system status, manage the lifecycle of end‑user technologies, enforce configuration standards, manage access in line with Group guidelines, implement required company software with responsible IT teams, provide troubleshooting support, and escalate issues to the IT Support team when needed;
Serve as the Key User for core systems - build and maintain internal know-how, create clear user guides, and deliver targeted trainings/consultations on new features and processes;
Requirements management - collect and document business needs, define functional and non-functional requirements for system improvements;
Integrations oversight - supervise API/integration health with insurers and other partners, ensure SSL certificates are renewed and provided for implementation on time;
Establishing and maintaining relations - building and sustaining effective collaboration with internal teams and third‑party partners, including external software vendors, insurance companies, responsible IT teams.
Our Offer:
The opportunity to work in a stable value-oriented company;
Experience and competence gained through training and development in an international company;
Flexible, trust‑based work set‑up and employee‑oriented organization (hybrid work module, additional incentive measures);
Employee insurance;
Company celebrations, team-building events and other activities;
The variable part of remuneration that depends on the results of work.
Your Profile:
University degree (preferably in IT, Business Management areas);
Proven experience as IT administrator, IT/Business analyst, IT project manager or similar roles;
Have a good understanding of business and IT processes;
Experience in prioritizing business requirements based on their value and developing good working relationships with clients and third-party suppliers.
Initiative and proactive attitude;
Analytical mindset, time‑management and collaboration skills
Working proficiency in Lithuanian and English;
Basic understanding of integrations and APIs.
Your personal data;
Please note that for the purpose of candidate selection, we process your personal data based on your consent, which you provide us with your CV, completed application forms and other data.
